{"ui_id":"u_000004_01","response_id":"r_000004_01","query_id":"q_000004","intent":"Recipe","tags":["recipe","meal_plan","vegetarian","steps"],"intent_bucket":"recipe","response_text":"# Speedy Paneer & Chickpea Curry Bowl\nMedia: Image=https://loremflickr.com/1200/800/paneer,curry Icon=https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap-icons@1.11.3/icons/cup-hot.svg\nA high-protein, satisfying vegetarian meal ready in under 40 minutes. This recipe combines creamy paneer, hearty chickpeas, and fresh spinach in a flavorful tomato-yogurt sauce, served over fluffy basmati rice. It's perfect for a healthy and quick weeknight dinner.\n\n## Ingredients & Nutrition Breakdown\nThis recipe serves 2 people.\n\n**For the Curry:**\n- **Paneer:** 250g, cut into 1-inch cubes\n- **Cooked Chickpeas:** 1 cup\n- **Fresh Spinach:** 3 cups, roughly chopped\n- **Tomato Puree:** 1 cup\n- **Greek Yogurt:** 1/2 cup\n- **Ginger-Garlic Paste:** 1 tbsp\n- **Garam Masala:** 1.5 tsp\n- **Turmeric Powder:** 1/2 tsp\n- **Cumin Seeds:** 1 tsp\n- **Lemon:** 1/2, juiced\n- **Oil or Ghee:** 1 tbsp\n- **Salt:** to taste\n\n**For Serving:**\n- **Basmati Rice:** 1 cup (uncooked)\n- **Water:** 2 cups (for rice)\n\n**Nutrition Estimate (per serving):**\n- **Calories:** ~650 kcal\n- **Protein:** **~38 g**\n- **Carbohydrates:** ~75 g\n- **Fat:** ~22 g\n\n## Step-by-Step Cooking Guide (35 Mins)\nMedia: Icon=https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap-icons@1.11.3/icons/stopwatch.svg\n\n### Step 1: Cook the Rice (Time: 0-20 mins)\n- Rinse 1 cup of basmati rice under cold water.\n- In a medium pot, combine the rinsed rice with 2 cups of water and a pinch of salt.\n- Bring to a boil, then reduce heat to the lowest setting, cover, and simmer for 15 minutes or until all water is absorbed.\n- Remove from heat and let it rest, covered, for 5 minutes. Fluff with a fork before serving.\n\n### Step 2: Sauté Aromatics & Spices (Time: 20-25 mins)\n- While the rice cooks, heat 1 tbsp of oil or ghee in a large pan or skillet over medium heat.\n- Add 1 tsp of cumin seeds and let them sizzle for 30 seconds until fragrant.\n- Stir in 1 tbsp of ginger-garlic paste and cook for another minute.\n- Pour in 1 cup of tomato puree, 1.5 tsp garam masala, 1/2 tsp turmeric, and salt to taste. Cook for 3-4 minutes, stirring occasionally, as the sauce thickens.\n\n### Step 3: Combine & Simmer (Time: 25-32 mins)\n- Add the 1 cup of cooked chickpeas and 3 cups of spinach to the pan. Stir until the spinach has wilted completely, which should take about 2-3 minutes.\n- Gently fold in the 250g of paneer cubes. Allow it to simmer for 2 more minutes to heat the paneer through and absorb the flavors of the sauce.\n\n### Step 4: Finish & Serve (Time: 32-35 mins)\n- Remove the pan from the heat. This is important to prevent the yogurt from curdling.\n- Stir in 1/2 cup of Greek yogurt and the juice of half a lemon until well combined and the sauce is creamy.\n- Divide the fluffy basmati rice between two bowls and top with the paneer and chickpea curry.\n\n## Quick Actions\nAction: [Button: Create Grocery List] https://anylist.com/\nAction: [Button: Start 35-Min Timer] https://www.google.com/search?q=set+a+timer+for+35+minutes\n\nIcons:\n- Alarm: https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap-icons@1.11.3/icons/alarm.svg\n- Book: https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap-icons@1.11.3/icons/book.svg","genui_json":{"root":"main","state":{"curry_ingredients":[{"item":"Paneer","quantity":"250g, cut into 1-inch cubes"},{"item":"Cooked Chickpeas","quantity":"1 cup"},{"item":"Fresh Spinach","quantity":"3 cups, roughly chopped"},{"item":"Tomato Puree","quantity":"1 cup"},{"item":"Greek Yogurt","quantity":"1/2 cup"},{"item":"Ginger-Garlic Paste","quantity":"1 tbsp"},{"item":"Garam Masala","quantity":"1.5 tsp"},{"item":"Turmeric Powder","quantity":"1/2 tsp"},{"item":"Cumin Seeds","quantity":"1 tsp"},{"item":"Lemon","quantity":"1/2, juiced"},{"item":"Oil or Ghee","quantity":"1 tbsp"},{"item":"Salt","quantity":"to taste"}],"serving_ingredients":[{"item":"Basmati Rice","quantity":"1 cup (uncooked)"},{"item":"Water","quantity":"2 cups (for rice)"}],"nutrition":[{"metric":"Calories","value":"~650 kcal"},{"metric":"Protein","value":"~38 g"},{"metric":"Carbohydrates","value":"~75 g"},{"metric":"Fat","value":"~22 g"}]},"elements":{"main":{"type":"Stack","props":{"direction":"vertical","gap":"lg"},"children":["title_stack","hero_image","intro_text","ingredients_card","steps_title_stack","step1_card","step2_card","step3_card","step4_card","actions_card"]},"title_stack":{"type":"Stack","props":{"direction":"horizontal","gap":"md","align":"center"},"children":["title_icon","title_text"]},"title_icon":{"type":"Icon","props":{"name":"../assets/r_000004_01_2_cup-hot.svg"},"children":[]},"title_text":{"type":"Text","props":{"text":"Speedy Paneer & Chickpea Curry Bowl","variant":"h2"},"children":[]},"hero_image":{"type":"Image","props":{"url":"../assets/r_000004_01_1_paneer_curry.jpg","fit":"cover"},"children":[]},"intro_text":{"type":"Text","props":{"text":"A high-protein, satisfying vegetarian meal ready in under 40 minutes. This recipe combines creamy paneer, hearty chickpeas, and fresh spinach in a flavorful tomato-yogurt sauce, served over fluffy basmati rice.","variant":"body"},"children":[]},"ingredients_card":{"type":"Card","props":{},"children":["ingredients_stack"]},"ingredients_stack":{"type":"Stack","props":{"direction":"vertical","gap":"md"},"children":["ingredients_title","servings_text","curry_ingredients_title","curry_ingredients_table","serving_ingredients_title","serving_ingredients_table","nutrition_title","nutrition_table"]},"ingredients_title":{"type":"Text","props":{"text":"Ingredients & Nutrition Breakdown","variant":"h2"},"children":[]},"servings_text":{"type":"Text","props":{"text":"This recipe serves 2 people.","variant":"caption"},"children":[]},"curry_ingredients_title":{"type":"Text","props":{"text":"For the Curry:","variant":"h3"},"children":[]},"curry_ingredients_table":{"type":"Table","props":